-- title:
--   Hecke modules on a cube-free level ladder with Taylor–Wiles levels
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal O$ is a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and $p$ is a prime with $p\neq 2$ whose image in $\mathcal O$ lies in the maximal ideal. Galois representations are taken of $G_{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ for $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q$; a valuation subring $P\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ *lies over* a prime $q$ when $q$ is a non-unit of $P$, $\sigma$ is a *Frobenius at $q$ for $P$* when $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition group of $P$ and induces $x\mapsto x^{q}$ on the residue field of $P$, and inertia means the image in $G_{\mathbb Q}$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$.
--
--   **Residual data.** $\bar\rho$ is a [`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22) over $k$: a two-dimensional $k$-vector space with a monoid homomorphism $G_{\mathbb Q}\to\mathrm{End}_k$ trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$. The hypothesis `habs` states that $\bar\rho$ becomes irreducible over $\overline{k}$. The hypothesis `hTW` strengthens this: for every field $K$ that is a $k$-algebra and every subgroup $G\le G_{\mathbb Q}$ of index $2$, any $K$-subspace of the base change $\bar\rho_K$ stable under $G$ is $\bot$ or $\top$.
--
--   **Sets of primes.** $S$ and $S_{\min}$ are finite sets of naturals with every element of $S$ prime (`hS`), $p\in S_{\min}$ (`hpSmin`), $S_{\min}\subseteq S$ (`hSmin`), and (`hmin`) a prime $q\neq p$ lies in $S_{\min}$ if and only if $\bar\rho$ is not unramified at $q$ (unramified meaning: for every $P$ lying over $q$, $\bar\rho(\sigma)=1$ for all $\sigma$ in inertia at $P$). The hypothesis `htame` states that the adic representation [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep ρbar`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196) is unipotent on inertia at every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$, i.e. the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $(X-1)^2$ for $\sigma$ in inertia at $q$.
--
--   **The ladder of levels.** $n\in\mathbb N$, a family of nonzero levels $N_k=\mathrm{Nf}\,k$ and a family of rung primes $q_k=\mathrm{qf}\,k$ are given, subject to: `hNS`, every prime dividing any $N_k$ lies in $S$; `hNp`, for $k\le n$ one has $p^2\nmid N_k$ and $p\mid N_k\iff p\mid N_n$; `hNmin`, for $k\le n$ every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N_k$; `hNunr`, for $k\le n$ every prime $q\neq p$ with $q\notin S_{\min}$ and $q\mid N_k$ satisfies $q^2\mid N_k$; `hN3`, for $k\le n$ no prime $q\neq p$ satisfies $q^3\mid N_k$; `hfoot`, $N_n$ is squarefree and the primes $q\neq p$ dividing $N_n$ all lie in $S_{\min}$; and `hrung`, for $k<n$ the number $q_k$ is prime, $q_k\neq p$, $q_k\in S$, and exactly one of the three shapes holds: $q_k\nmid N_{k+1}$ and $N_k=N_{k+1}q_k^2$; or $q_k\mid N_{k+1}$, $q_k^2\nmid N_{k+1}$ and $N_k=N_{k+1}q_k$; or $q_k^2\mid N_{k+1}$ and $N_k=N_{k+1}q_k$. For each $k$ the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N_k)$ are assumed to have an integral structure, i.e. [`CuspForm.intLattice`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) (the $\mathbb Z$-span of the forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers) spans the whole space over $\mathbb C$.
--
--   **Hecke data.** For a level $N$, `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` is the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$; and `heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ` is the localisation of the $\mathcal O$-base change `heckeBaseAlgebra N S 𝒪` of the Hecke lattice at the multiplicative set of images of the elements outside the prime ideal `heckeCharKernel` cut out by a character $\theta$, i.e. the local Hecke algebra attached to the mod-$p$ eigensystem $\theta$. Write $T_k=\,$`heckeLocal (Nf k) S 𝒪 (θf k)`.
--
--   The data are: ring homomorphisms $\theta_k=\mathrm{\theta f}\,k:\$`heckeAlgebra (Nf k) 2 S`$\to k$ with (`hθ`) the property that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N_k$ and $\ell\notin S$, every $P$ lying over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2-\theta_k(T_\ell)X+\ell$; a ring homomorphism $\chi:\$`heckeAlgebra (Nf n) 2 S`$\to\mathcal O$ lifting $\theta_n$ (`hχ`: $\mathrm{residue}\circ\chi=\theta_n$); $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms $\pi_k:T_k\to\mathcal O$ with (`hπT`) $\pi_k$ applied to the image of $T_\ell$ in $T_k$ equal to $\chi(T_\ell)$ whenever $k\le n$, $\ell\notin S$ is prime and $\ell$ divides neither $N_k$ nor $N_n$; and a family $a:\mathbb N\to\mathcal O$ such that (`ha`) for every $k<n$ with $q_k\nmid N_{k+1}$ there is a rank-two adic representation $\rho'$ over $\mathcal O$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at all primes $\ell\nmid N_{k+1}$, $\ell\notin S$, are $X^2-\pi_{k+1}(T_\ell)X+\ell$, which is unramified at $q_k$, and whose Frobenius trace at $q_k$ equals $a_k$. Finally $H_n$ is a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) for level $N_n$, set $S$, ring $\mathcal O$, character $\theta_n$ and ring $T_n$: a homomorphism $\pi:\$`heckeAlgebra (Nf n) 2 S`$\to T_n$ reducing to $\theta_n$, with $T_n$ generated over $\mathcal O$ by the image of $\pi$, with every $\mathcal O$-valued Hecke character lifting $\theta_n$ factoring through $\pi$, with $\mathrm{residue}\circ(\mathcal O\to T_n)$ surjective, together with a rank-two adic representation $H_n.\rho$ over $T_n$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials are $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist types $M_k$ ($k\in\mathbb N$) carrying abelian group structures, $T_k$-module structures, $\mathcal O$-module structures forming a scalar tower $\mathcal O\to T_k\to M_k$, each $M_k$ finite and free over $\mathcal O$, together with $\mathcal O$-bilinear pairings $B_k:M_k\times M_k\to\mathcal O$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (i) For $k\le n$ the pairing is Hecke-self-adjoint: $B_k(tm,m')=B_k(m,tm')$ for all $t\in T_k$ and $m,m'\in M_k$.
--
--   (ii) For $k\le n$ the induced map $M_k\to\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(M_k,\mathcal O)$ is bijective, i.e. $B_k$ is perfect.
--
--   (iii) For $k\le n$ the submodule of $M_k$ annihilated by every element of $\ker\pi_k$ is non-zero.
--
--   (iv) For $k\le n$, $\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal O}M_k$ equals the $\mathcal O$-rank of that $\ker\pi_k$-torsion submodule multiplied by $\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal O}T_k$.
--
--   (v) For every $k<n$ there exist $\mathcal O$-linear maps $i:M_{k+1}\to M_k$ and $j:M_k\to M_{k+1}$ and an element $\Delta\in T_{k+1}$ such that: $B_{k+1}(j\,m',m)=B_k(m',i\,m)$ for all $m'\in M_k$, $m\in M_{k+1}$; $j(i\,m)=\Delta\cdot m$ for all $m\in M_{k+1}$; $i$ carries the $\ker\pi_{k+1}$-torsion submodule of $M_{k+1}$ onto the $\ker\pi_k$-torsion submodule of $M_k$ (as $\mathcal O$-submodules); $\pi_{k+1}(\Delta)\neq 0$; if $q_k\nmid N_{k+1}$ then $(q_k-1)\bigl(a_k^2-(q_k+1)^2\bigr)$ divides $\pi_{k+1}(\Delta)$ in $\mathcal O$; and if $q_k\mid N_{k+1}$ but $q_k^2\nmid N_{k+1}$ then $q_k^2-1$ divides $\pi_{k+1}(\Delta)$.
--
--   (vi) (Taylor–Wiles level, strict ordinary case.) Assume $p\mid N_n$ and that the adic representation attached to $\bar\rho$ is not flat at $p$, i.e. `IsFlatAt p` fails (flatness at $p$ asking that the residue field be finite and that, for every ideal $I$ of the coefficient ring with finite quotient, the finite Galois module $V/IV$ be the group of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of a finite flat commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring `ratLocalizedAt p` of rationals with denominator coprime to $p$). Let $r\in\mathbb N$ and let $qv:\mathrm{Fin}\,r\to\mathbb N$ be injective with each $qv_i$ prime, $qv_i\notin S$ and $p\mid qv_i-1$, and assume that at each $qv_i$ Frobenius has distinct eigenvalues: for every $P$ lying over $qv_i$ and every Frobenius $\varphi$ at $qv_i$ for $P$ the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\varphi)$ factors as $(X-\alpha)(X-\beta)$ with $\alpha\neq\beta$ in $k$. Let $D_{\min}$ be a [`GaloisRep.DeformationRingData`](def/GaloisRep_DeformationRingData.html#L8) for $\bar\rho$ over $\mathcal O$ for the condition `minimalStrictOrdinaryCondition 𝒪 p Smin` (cyclotomic determinant at $p$, strict ordinarity at $p$, unramified outside $S_{\min}$, and unipotent on inertia at every prime $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$), and let $D_Q$ be such a datum for the condition asking `strictOrdinaryCondition 𝒪 p (Smin ∪ qv(Fin r))` together with unipotence on inertia at every prime $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$; each such datum consists of a complete noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $R$ with local structure map and surjective residue map, a rank-two adic representation over $R$ of the prescribed type whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$, universal for these properties. Let $\phi:D_{\min}.R\to T_n$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map which is a local homomorphism and such that the base change of $D_{\min}.\rho$ along $\phi$ is equivalent to $H_n.\rho$. Let $\mathrm{cyc}$ assign to each natural $q$ a homomorphism $G_{\mathbb Q}\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, let $\pi_\Delta$ assign to each $q$ a homomorphism $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q-1)}$ (written multiplicatively), let $\varepsilon:D_Q.R\to D_{\min}.R$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map and let $\iota$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from the monoid algebra $\mathcal O[\Delta]$, $\Delta=\prod_{i<r}\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(qv_i-1)}$ written multiplicatively, into $D_Q.R$, subject to: $\mathrm{cyc}(q)$ describes the Galois action on $q$-th roots of unity for prime $q$ ($\sigma\mu=\mu^{(\mathrm{cyc}(q)\sigma).\mathrm{val}}$ whenever $\mu^q=1$); $\pi_\Delta(q)$ is surjective for every prime $q\neq p$; $\varepsilon$ is a local homomorphism along which $D_Q.\rho$ base changes to a representation equivalent to $D_{\min}.\rho$; $\varepsilon(\iota(g))=1$ for every group-like basis element $g$ of $\mathcal O[\Delta]$; $\ker\varepsilon$ is the ideal generated by the elements $\iota(g)-1$; and, for each $i$ and each $P$ lying over $qv_i$, there is a $D_Q.R$-basis $b_0,b_1$ of $D_Q.\rho.V$ in which inertia at $P$ acts diagonally through $\iota$, by $\iota\bigl(\mathrm{mulSingle}_i\,\pi_\Delta(qv_i)(\mathrm{cyc}(qv_i)\sigma)\bigr)$ on $b_0$ and by the inverse character on $b_1$. Then there exists a type $M^{(n)}$ with an abelian group structure, a $D_Q.R$-module structure, an $\mathcal O[\Delta]$-module structure, an $\mathcal O$-module structure forming a scalar tower $\mathcal O\to\mathcal O[\Delta]\to M^{(n)}$, such that $M^{(n)}$ is non-trivial, finite over $\mathcal O$, free over $\mathcal O[\Delta]$, the $\mathcal O[\Delta]$-action is the $D_Q.R$-action through $\iota$ ($c\cdot m=\iota(c)\cdot m$), and there is an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ from the quotient of $M^{(n)}$ by the augmentation submodule $\ker(\text{counit of }\mathcal O[\Delta])\cdot M^{(n)}$ onto $M_n$ satisfying $e(\overline{x\cdot m})=\phi(\varepsilon(x))\cdot e(\overline m)$ for all $x\in D_Q.R$ and $m\in M^{(n)}$.
--
--   (vii) (Taylor–Wiles level, flat case.) The same assertion as (vii) holds under the hypothesis $p\nmid N_n$ (no flatness hypothesis on $\bar\rho$ being imposed), with the deformation conditions replaced by their flat analogues: $D_{\min}$ a deformation datum for `minimalFlatCondition 𝒪 p Smin` (cyclotomic determinant at $p$, flatness at $p$, unramified outside $S_{\min}$, unipotent on inertia at the primes $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$) and $D_Q$ one for `flatCondition 𝒪 p (Smin ∪ qv(Fin r))` together with unipotence on inertia at the primes $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$; the remaining hypotheses on $qv$, $\phi$, $\mathrm{cyc}$, $\pi_\Delta$, $\varepsilon$, $\iota$ and the conclusion about $M^{(n)}$ are word for word those of (vi).
--
--   This is the Hecke-module input to the Taylor–Wiles method: it produces, along a ladder of cube-free levels interpolating between the minimal level of $\bar\rho$ and the level $N_n$, self-dual Hecke modules of rank one over the local Hecke algebras, Ihara-type maps whose composite is multiplication by an element with a prescribed $\eta$-divisibility, and, at auxiliary Taylor–Wiles level, modules free over the group algebra of the $p$-part of $\prod(\mathbb Z/qv_i)^\times$ whose coinvariants recover the module at level $N_n$ — in the strict ordinary and in the flat case according to whether $p$ divides $N_n$. It is the variant of the corresponding statement in which the levels are additionally assumed cube-free away from $p$ (hypothesis `hN3`), and it feeds the proofs that the Hecke pairing is bijective with an explicit presentation and the construction of the patching data used in the modularity lifting theorem.
